<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Volodar Rostyslavych</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1124">1124</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Volodar of Peremyshl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Volodar Rostyslavych was a Rurikid prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl">Peremyshl</a>, now Przemyśl, in south-western Rus'. With his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a> and Vasylko he took control of the towns of the region in the 1080s and defended them against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. His son Volodymyrko later united these lands as the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/volodar-rostyslavych.jpg" alt="Volodar Rostyslavych" width="320" height="303" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Europe_mediterranean_1190_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
